Z||000001||StuGood||07-20-2001||06:34 PM||stuart@southwind.net||You meant IAC (idle air control), not sensor, I think.  Might remove the existing idle  sensor (Oops! I meant IAC  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), and see if it and the air passages in the throttle body need cleaning.  I believe if you remove the flexible air intake hose from the throttle body, the opening you'll see at the base of the throttle body's throat, is the one it breathes through, for idle air.||12.13.248.4||reg||1
